  "prompts": {
    "EXPLAIN_INSTRUCTION": "Explain in 2-4 sentences, for a test engineer, what this test checks, why it matters for the requirement, and what outcome is expected. Do not invent byte values.",
    "PARSE_INSTRUCTION": "Extract the UDS identifiers that requirement_text mentions or clearly implies, using only keys from spec_index. services must never be empty: always name the service whose behaviour the requirement specifies. Do not add DIDs, routines or services the text does not refer to.\nPhrase -> identifier guide:\n- read/report a value -> 0x22; write/set/store/change a value or calibration -> 0x2E\n- switch/enter/return to a session or mode -> 0x10\n- default session -> session 0x01; programming/flash/bootloader -> session 0x02; extended/diagnostic mode -> session 0x03\n- unlock, seed/key, security access -> 0x27; 'security level 1' -> level 0x01; programming-level unlock -> level 0x03\n- ECU reset/reboot -> 0x11; keep-alive/tester present -> 0x3E\n- start/stop/results of a routine or self-test -> 0x31 plus the routine id\n- read fault memory/trouble codes -> 0x19; clear them -> 0x14\n- a named setting or value (VIN, wiper sensitivity, brightness...) -> the DID in spec_index with that name\nAdd 0x10 and/or 0x27 to services only when a session or an unlock is a condition of the behaviour ('shall require extended session', 'after unlocking'). 'In any/every session' is not a condition: fill sessions, do not add 0x10. Fill sessions and security_levels whenever they are named or implied.\nExample: 'Changing the ambient colour shall need extended mode and a level 1 unlock.' -> services [0x10, 0x27, 0x2E], dids [0x0101], sessions [0x03], security_levels [0x01], intents [write, security, session].\nExample: 'The part number shall be readable in every session.' -> services [0x22], dids [0xF187], sessions [0x01, 0x02, 0x03], intents [read, positive].",
    "PLAN_INSTRUCTION": "Choose test cases that verify the requirement thoroughly: positive behaviour plus negative, session, security and timing checks where relevant. Each choice is a template_id from the catalog and an option_index from that template's options, with a one-sentence rationale. Do not repeat choices listed under rejected or already_kept.",
    "SCHEMA_RETRY_INSTRUCTION": "Your previous reply was not valid JSON for the required schema. Error: {error}\nReply again with only a JSON object that matches the schema.",
    "SYSTEM_PROMPT": "You are a UDS (ISO 14229) diagnostics test-planning assistant for an automotive ECU. You never write request or response bytes. You only reference identifiers that exist in the provided spec index, choose template ids and option indices from the provided catalog, and write short plain-English prose. Answer with JSON matching the schema when one is required."
  },
